Fix GDMS request signing - wrong param name, missing token-call signature (v0.119)

Live testing against BNS's real GDMS account surfaced two separate
mistakes in the signing implementation, both producing the same
"signature not exists" error:

1. The signature was sent as a query parameter named "sign" - GDMS's
   own Common Parameters doc names the field "signature". Every GDMS
   call (not just login) was sending it under the wrong name, so GDMS
   never found the parameter it required.

2. "Getting Token"/"Refreshing Token" (/oauth/token) also need their
   own timestamp+signature, which their per-endpoint parameter table
   doesn't show. A separate sentence on the Common Parameters page -
   "not required to be carried except for Getting Token interface and
   Refreshing Token interface" - is a double negative meaning those
   two endpoints are exactly the ones that DO need it, signing their
   own request params (username/password/grant_type/client_id/
   client_secret for Getting Token; refresh_token/grant_type/
   client_id/client_secret for Refreshing Token) plus timestamp,
   rather than the usual fixed four-param set every other endpoint
   uses.

GdmsSignatureUtil gains a general calculateSignature(SortedMap,
jsonBody) overload that signs whatever param set is handed to it; the
original four-common-param version is now a thin wrapper around it.
GdmsAuthService#login()/refresh() build and sign their own param sets
and add timestamp/signature to the /oauth/token query string.
GdmsChannelService#post() corrected to send "signature" instead of
"sign".

gdms-api-findings.md (project doc) updated with both fixes and the
corrected algorithm.

